        "original_id": "192bdf51-ad11-5c2e-992d-4f78676e5e39",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness; Charles Edward Stuart; Henry Benedict Stuart; James Francis Edward Stuart; Ignazio Busca\n- Events: Jacobite uprising of 1745; Battle of Culloden\n- Roles: titular archbishop of Emesa\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Edward Stuart instigated the unsuccessful Jacobite uprising of 1745 and led an insurrection to restore his family to the throne of Great Britain.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was a Perthshire gentleman who joined Charles Edward Stuart's 1745 rebellion, was captured at the Battle of Culloden, and was later convicted of treason.\n- Unlike his father James Francis Edward Stuart and his brother Charles Edward Stuart, Henry Benedict Stuart made no effort to seize the throne.\n- On September 17, 1775, Henry Benedict Stuart consecrated Ignazio Busca in Frascati after Busca was elected titular archbishop of Emesa.",
